{
  "assumptions": [
    "The data records arrival, first clinician contact and departure, but never when treatment ended, so `departure - seen` is clinician time PLUS everything else the visit contains (tests, results, boarding). The split is not identifiable from these columns. It is estimated as a single free parameter -- the fraction of post-contact time during which a doctor is occupied -- chosen so that simulated mean wait matches observed. A multiplicative fraction rather than a constant offset, because with this roster the department could not function if a doctor were occupied for the whole visit: all post-contact time would require 4.95x the rostered capacity. The split preserves treatment + boarding = post_contact exactly, so length of stay remains an independent validation metric.",
    "Patience is only observed for patients who ran out of it; everyone who was seen had patience longer than their wait, which is censoring. The shape is taken from the observed time-to-abandon per acuity level and the scale is then fitted so the simulated abandonment rate matches the observed one.",
    "Mean wait and the overall abandonment rate were USED to fit the two free parameters, so their agreement is guaranteed by construction and is not evidence. Every other row of the validation table -- p90 wait, length of stay, the per-acuity waits and the per-acuity abandonment rates -- was held out of the fit and is genuine out-of-sample validation."
  ],
